    "body": "## What\n\n`_init_ipc_manager` links the `cuda_ipc` JIT module with a bare `-lcuda`. Where `libcuda.so` isn't on the linker search path, the build fails (`ld: cannot find -lcuda`); `parallel_state.py` catches it with a warning and continues with custom allreduce disabled, so affected setups fall back to NCCL (~5x slower per call in the incident we measured). Fix: use `cuda_stubs_dir()`, same as `dsv4/wo_a.py` and `kda_ptx_prefill`.\n\n## Why it wasn't caught before\n\nNot a recent regression — bare `-lcuda` dates to the v2 rewrite (#31049). It's masked only in images that symlink the stub into the system libdir (AOT, sgl-deep-ep). The main `docker/Dockerfile` (release + dev images) doesn't; we hit it on a dev-image GB300 box with no `/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libcuda.so`.\n\nSibling with the same flags: `vsa_block_sparse_sm100_jit.py` (untouched here — different subsystem, source-level exposure only).\n\n## Verification (GB300, previously failing)\n\n- old flags → build fails (control)\n- fixed flags → links, `register_once()` succeeds\n- no change where the link already worked\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #38215697708](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38215697708)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38215697247](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38215697247)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #38215697932](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38215697932)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
